-- title:
--   Level automorphisms on the level field and its j-charts, q=2
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime with $q = 2$, let $M' \ge 1$ with $q \nmid M'$, and assume $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M' \le \mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$, i.e. the base change to $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ of the full level-$M'$ modular function field sits inside $F := \mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ (the $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-base changed $x_H$-function field of level $q^2M'$ for the subgroup $\mathrm{levelH}\,q\,M'$), realised inside $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}})$. Let $k_0 \subseteq \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ be an intermediate field of $\mathbb{Q}$, let $K_1$ be a $k_0$-intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ that is finite over $k_0$, and let $A_1$ be a valuation subring of $K_1$. Give $F$ its $k_0$-algebra structure through $\overline{\mathbb{Q}} \to F$. Then for every $k_0$-intermediate field $F_0$ of $F$ such that (i) $k_0(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}) \sqcup F_0 = F$, where $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ means the range of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}} \to F$; (ii) $F_0$ is stable under $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta'\,\gamma$ for every primitive $q$-th root of unity index $\zeta' : \mathrm{Idx}\,q$ and every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$; (iii) for every $k_0$-intermediate field $K'$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ finite over $k_0$, every finite family $c : \mathrm{Fin}\,m \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ that is $K'$-linearly independent and every family $a$ of elements of $T' := k_0(\text{image of } K') \sqcup F_0$ with $\sum_i c_i a_i = 0$ has all $a_i = 0$; and (iv) every element of $F$ whose Laurent series lies in the range of $\mathrm{coeffEmb}\,\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ (that is, has coefficients in $\mathbb{Q}$) lies in $F_0$; and for every $A_1$-algebra structure on $T_1 := k_0(\text{image of }K_1) \sqcup F_0$ whose structure map is induced by $A_1 \subseteq K_1 \subseteq \overline{\mathbb{Q}} \to F$; and for every $j_1 \in T_1$ whose image in $F$ is the element with Laurent series $\mathrm{coeffEmb}\,\overline{\mathbb{Q}}\,\mathrm{jq}$: there exists $j' \in T_1$ with Laurent series $\mathrm{coeffEmb}\,\overline{\mathbb{Q}}\,(\mathrm{qExpand}\,\mathbb{Q}\,q\,\mathrm{jq})$, the $q$-expansion of $j$ with all exponents multiplied by $q$, such that $j'$ lies in the chart subalgebra $\mathrm{chartAlgFin}\,A_1\,T_1\,j_1$ attached to $j_1$, $j_1$ lies in $\mathrm{chartAlgFin}\,A_1\,T_1\,j'$, and every $g$ in the subgroup of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-algebra automorphisms of $F$ generated by the automorphisms $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta\,\gamma$ ($\zeta : \mathrm{Idx}\,q$, $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$) admits an $A_1$-algebra automorphism $\sigma$ of $T_1$ with: $\sigma$ and $\sigma^{-1}$ agree with $g$ and $g^{-1}$ on $T_1$ after inclusion into $F$; $\sigma(j') = j'$; $\sigma$ preserves membership in $\mathrm{chartAlgFin}\,A_1\,T_1\,j_1$ and in $\mathrm{chartAlgInf}\,A_1\,T_1\,j'$ in both directions; and for every place $P$ of $F$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ (a valuation subring of $F$, not all of $F$, containing the image of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ and a principal ideal ring) that is rational, in the sense that $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ surjects onto its residue field, the translate $g \cdot P$ is again rational and satisfies $(g\cdot P).\mathrm{evalAt}(g f) = P.\mathrm{evalAt}\,f$ and $g f \in (g \cdot P)$'s valuation subring iff $f$ lies in $P$'s, for all $f \in F$.
--
--   This is the $q = 2$ case of the descent statement that the level automorphisms of the full-level modular function field restrict to automorphisms of the $K_1$-form $T_1 = K_1 \cdot F_0$ over the valuation ring $A_1$, fixing the function with $q$-expansion $j(q\tau)$ and preserving both charts of the two-chart integral model as well as rationality of places; in classical terms it records the field of definition of the level automorphisms together with the integrality of the modular equation relating $j$ and $j(q\tau)$. It feeds the Igusa-tower leg of the semistable covering argument, being used in the comparison of Igusa rings and in the constructions producing level translates of centred points of the two-chart integral model.
